            <ArticleTitle>Patient education and self-advocacy: queries and responses on pain management; erythromelalgia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>295-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/15360280903099067</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Questions from patients concerning a disease process known as erythromelalgia, its diagnosis, symptoms, and treatments are answered to help patients and caregivers understand the disease and its treatment. The responses from the author are intended to educate patients about their disease and make them more effective self-advocates.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
